PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains a unanimous consensus on Choice D (Positive linear relationship between VEGF and Weeke white matter score). The selection is supported methodologically because the Weeke white matter score provides a continuous quantitative metric appropriate for parametric linear regression modeling, unlike the ordinal Barkovich or NICHD scales. Neuropathologically, acute hypoxia-induced VEGF functions as a microvascular permeability factor that correlates directly with vulnerable white matter injury in neonatal encephalopathy. Competing options proposing inverse relationships or pairing inflammatory markers with ordinal scales remain methodologically and biologically inconsistent.
}

